# The converters' JSON output, read by emit-contract.cjs. Rebuilt, not committed:
# `exported_powers/` IS committed, so a clone with no game install regenerates the whole
# tree with `npm run regen`. Committing it would put an 80 MB derived copy beside the
# 694 MB it derives from, with nothing checking they agree.
#
# Nothing authored or vendored lives in here, and that is the rule that keeps this safe to
# delete: `hand-data/` and `mids-tables/` are read where they sit, never copied in.
/pipeline/

# Node (pipeline scripts). Unanchored and without the trailing slash: a worktree that
# borrows a sibling checkout's install has `node_modules` as a SYMLINK, which `node_modules/`
# does not match, so it showed up as untracked and one `git add -A` from being committed.
node_modules

# Rust — anchored: an unanchored `target/` also swallowed the pet-target export
# directories (exported_powers/*/pets/target), silently leaving real export data
# untracked.
/target/

# SECURITY_AUDIT.md F87. The anchor above is right and the hole it leaves is real: every
# NON-root crate has a `target/` the anchor does not reach, and `dioxus.toml`'s
# `out_dir = "target/dx"` is resolved by dx against the CRATE directory, so `dx bundle`
# copies each finished bundle into `crates/app/target/dx` — inside the source tree.
# 3,492 files and a 41.6 MB Mach-O got committed that way in 682c3e32 before anyone noticed.
# Listed per crate rather than as an unanchored `target/`, because unanchoring is the thing
# the comment above forbids. `scripts/keys/no-crate-target-tracked.py` fails when a crate is
# added to the workspace and not added here.
/crates/*/target/
/vendor/*/target/

# Python (bin-crawler / pigg-wrangler tooling)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dioxus
dist/
.dioxus/

# Local scratch / env
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Machine-local cargo config (libxdo path)
.cargo/

# Planning and notes, reference
bins/
# Moved out of the tree on 2026-09-24 with the two below — see tools/refdata.py.
raw defs/

# Manual mids-oracle canonical dump — regenerable cache, 14 MB (see tools/mids-oracle/README.md)
tools/mids-oracle/.oracle_cache/

# Playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/
/playwright/.auth/

# Playwright MCP snapshot artifacts
/.playwright-mcp/

#Other
.impeccable/

# Understand-analysis output. The graph it produced was a one-shot snapshot that
# rotted (54% of the files it described had moved or vanished within 3 weeks), and
# nothing was ignoring its scratch dir, so 6.4 MB of generator trash got committed.
# If the tool is ever run again, this keeps its output local.
.ua/

# cargo-mutants run output; CI uploads it as an artifact instead.
mutants.out*/

# Reference inputs that used to be vendored here and are NOT any more (2026-09-24).
# They live in a tree beside the repo now — see tools/refdata.py, which is the one
# place that says where, and COH_REFDATA / COH_RAW_DEFS, which relocate it.
#
# Kept as ignores rather than deleted, because the failure they prevent is silent:
# a gitignored directory inside the tree resolves to nothing on a fresh checkout,
# and every gate over it self-skips, which reads exactly like a pass. If one of
# these trees is ever dropped back in, it stays untracked instead of being
# committed and quietly becoming the default again.
#
# `/Thunderspy/` is ANCHORED and must stay that way. Unanchored it matches at
# any depth, and with core.ignorecase it also swallows
# src/data/datasets/thunderspy/ — tracked files there keep working, so only NEW
# files go silently un-added. That is how a Thunderspy-only fix ships as a no-op.
MidsReborn-master/
/Thunderspy/

# Tooling activity log — local session bookkeeping, not project state.
/.pi/

# Debug scratch (probes, .bak snapshots, test-run logs). Individual probe
# scripts get force-added and tracked when a committed comment or doc cites
# them by path as census evidence. No committed comment cites one today.
/.scratch/

# `ruff check` (npm run lint:py) writes its cache here. Added with the gate, 2026-09-26;
# it had been sitting untracked and unignored since somebody ran ruff by hand on 2026-09-20.
.ruff_cache/

# AI agent files: instructions, skills, settings and tool output, for Claude and other
# coding assistants. All of it stays local. The shared copies live outside the repo,
# in ../.claude/skills/ and ../next/, versioned by the parent folder's own git repo.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.claude/
.agents/
.mcp.json
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.windsurf/
.windsurfrules
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.aider*
.codex/
.gemini/
.continue/
.clinerules
.roo/
.ua/
.ori/
.pi/
.playwright-mcp/
